Recursive K-Group Reversal - O(n) Time and O(n/k) SpaceThe idea is to reverse the first k nodes of the list and update the head of the list to the new head of this reversed segment. Then, connect the tail of this reversed segment to the result of recursively reversing the remaining portion of the list.If the list is empty, return head.Traverse the next k nodes using temp to find the starting node of the next group. Reverse the current k nodes using reverseKNodes(), which reverses the links one by one. The original head becomes the tail of the reversed group, so connect it to the result of recursively processing the remaining list. Recursively call reverseKGroup(temp, k) for the next group. Return the new head (groupHead) of the reversed list.
